"""Reviewed task content for Brotato. Editorial interpretation is identified in-page."""
STORE='https://store.steampowered.com/app/4498220/Brotato_Primal_Dread/'
BASE='https://store.steampowered.com/app/1942280/Brotato/'
NEWS='https://steamcommunity.com/app/1942280/announcements/?l=english'
PRESS='https://app.pressengine.net/newsdesk/futurefriendsgames'
TIPS='https://www.reddit.com/r/brotato/comments/1xqowut/thoughts_and_tips_on_primal_dread_dlc_mechanics/'
CAVE='https://www.reddit.com/r/brotato/comments/1xn1a3j/i_love_everything_in_this_update_except_this/'
HOTFIX='https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1849192144187249'
BALANCE='https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1849192144183252'
BETA='https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1848664643359916'
GUIDE='https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2896126855&l=english'
def link(u,t):return f'<a href="{u}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{t} ↗<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>'
def p(t):return '<p>'+t+'</p>'
def table(h,rows):return '<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Comparison table, scroll horizontally"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+x+'</th>'for x in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+x+'</td>'for x in r)+'</tr>'for r in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
PAGES=[
('evolution','Brotato Evolution Guide — Choose Mecha or Mutation', 'Choose a Brotato Evolution path by build, enemy hazards and branch. Separate launch mechanics from November beta balance changes.', 'Choose Mecha to direct upgrades into weapons. Consider Mutation when item effects carry your run. Both directions also change enemies and their hazards.', 'mecha',[
('choose','Choose by what carries your run',table(['Your run','Consider','Reason'],[['Strong weapon core','Mecha','Choose reinforcement stats for the weapon plan.'],['Strong passive item package','Mutation','Random copied effects can develop that package.'],['Dying before scaling','Immediate survival','An unfinished scaling plan cannot rescue a dead run.']])+p('This is our editorial framework based on the '+link(NEWS,'developer’s Evolution explanation')+'. It is not a measured ranking.')),
('drops','Follow the drops and watch the hazards',p('Mecha parts feed weapon reinforcement. The launch post also describes dismantling mecha weapons for additional parts. Mutation copies item effects randomly. Inspect the actual result before building your next shop decision around it.')+p('Mecha enemies introduce lasers and slowing oil. Mutant enemies spread acid. Leave an exit lane instead of crossing a puddle to collect every drop. Directed upgrades can be easier to plan around, while random copies require checking what the run actually gained.')),
('branch','Read the branch before copying a build',p('The 12 November Balancing Patch brings the tested Evolution changes to the Steam default branch. Mechanization grants +3% weapon damage per mecha power point, previously +5%. At eight mechanizations a weapon deals 208% of its base damage, previously 280%. Extra piercing and bounces are removed. Stat bonuses stop growing after rank eight, and Mecha Parts drop chance falls from 2% to 1.5%. Budget crowd coverage separately. Older launch builds and the 6 and 10 November beta notes describe earlier stages of these changes. '+link(BALANCE,'12 November balance notes'))),
('mutation-beta','Inspect Mutation results after the balance patch',p('Each mutation now puts its -1 Evolution on the Tumor. An item becomes mutant when it loses a negative modifier, and duplicate Tumor effects merge into one line. Mutation Fruit base drop chance rises from 3% to 4%, then falls by one percentage point every ten waves from wave 30, to a minimum of 1%. Inspect the Tumor when checking what a mutation changed. '+link(BALANCE,'12 November balance notes'))),
('snowball','Snowball after hotfix 1.2.0.3',p('Snowball now grants Elemental Damage only for items bought in the shop or found in crates. Tumor mutations no longer grant extra Elemental Damage on every mutation. Keep that distinction in mind when valuing another mutation for an elemental build. '+link(HOTFIX,'1.2.0.3 hotfix notes'))),
('shop','Make the next shop decision',p('If you lack damage, compare an immediate weapon upgrade with reinforcement. If collection is killing you, buy enough movement or defense to reach the next wave. With Mutation, inspect copied effects rather than assuming the best passive was selected. Reassess when the actual build changes.'))]),
('caveman','Brotato Caveman Build — Plan the Primitive Weapon Slot','Use a reported Caveman spear route and keep room for the Primitive-weapon shop cycle. Account for permanent fog and source limitations.', 'Plan the shop cycle before filling every slot. Two community reports describe five working weapons and a sixth slot for buying and burning a Primitive weapon. Spears are one reported route.', 'steam-3',[
('loop','Keep the purchase slot usable',p('The '+link(TIPS,'jldark89 report')+' uses five Spears as the working core and a temporary sixth weapon for the cycle. The '+link(CAVE,'earlier Caveman discussion')+' describes a similar slot plan with axes. Both are launch-week player reports. Confirm the current trait and qualifying weapon class on your character sheet.')+'<ol><li>Read which weapons qualify as Primitive.</li><li>Build a core that can clear the next wave without its temporary purchase.</li><li>Lock a suitable future purchase when available.</li><li>Complete the burn action in the shop and inspect the effect before leaving.</li></ol>'),
('core','Spend on weapons you will keep',p('Spears are the starting hypothesis from the newer report. Axes are an alternative in the earlier thread. Invest upgrades in the working core and preserve enough materials for the cycle. These reports establish a practical slot-management approach, not a universal best weapon or a guaranteed Nightmare clear.')),
('fog','Account for permanent fog',p('The 1.2.0.3 hotfix removes Boomerang from Caveman’s starting weapons, reversing the 12 November addition. The visibility tooltip for his permanent fog remains part of the 12 November changes. The reported Spear route remains a launch-week strategy. Reduced visibility makes chasing drops riskier. Judge an exit before committing to a path. '+link(NEWS,'Developer notes'))),
('beta','Mutation after the balance patch',p('The 12 November default-branch patch excludes Mutation copies of Caveman’s weapon-burning effect. Keep the shop cycle grounded in the character’s own ability. '+link(BALANCE,'12 November balance notes'))),
('failure','If the cycle keeps failing',p('Check weapon class, spare slot and purchase budget. If the cycle works but the next wave still kills you, improve the working core or learn the fog on a lower difficulty. A successful shop interaction alone does not show that the loadout can survive.'))]),
('veteran','Brotato Veteran Build — Ranged Route and Healing Checks','Plan a source-based Veteran ranged route for Primal Dread. Check healing restrictions, crowd coverage and launch-week weapon recommendations.', 'Start with a coherent ranged plan and read healing restrictions before buying sustain. A launch-week player recommends Machine Gun with flat Ranged Damage, Range and piercing. Treat it as a reported route.', 'veteran',[
('route','Support the gun you can use',p('The '+link(TIPS,'jldark89 report')+' recommends Machine Gun with ranged scaling and piercing for crowds. Its author plays Nightmare with wave retries enabled. That context matters when judging how forgiving the route is.')+p('Buy for the next problem. Groups reaching you call for crowd coverage and attack uptime. An elite living too long calls for inspecting weapon scaling and time spent firing. The advice here is editorial interpretation of that reported route.')),
('healing','Check restrictions before buying recovery',p('The '+link(NEWS,'official launch post')+' presents Veteran as a swarm-fighting character without time to heal. Read the exact current character sheet before buying HP regeneration, Life Steal or between-wave recovery. A bonus to a blocked recovery method may offer little value.')+p('Check any missing-health bonus on your installed version before intentionally fighting hurt. Leave enough health to survive an unexpected hit. We do not reproduce unverified numerical traits from launch-week summary sites.')),
('shop','A Veteran shop checklist','<ol><li>Concentrate weapons around the damage stat you are buying.</li><li>Check whether crowds die before reaching you.</li><li>Preserve a retreat lane with movement and defense.</li><li>Read restrictions before buying recovery.</li><li>Record map, difficulty, branch and active Item Sets when comparing builds.</li></ol>'),
('evolution','Choose Evolution after the core works',p('A weapon-focused route gives a reason to inspect Mecha reinforcement, while Mutation develops passives. After the 12 November Steam balance patch, mechanization grants +3% weapon damage per mecha power point and supplies no extra piercing or bounces. Check crowd coverage before investing in reinforcement. Use the <a href="/brotato/evolution/">Evolution guide</a> against your current tooltips.'))]),
('co-op','Brotato Co-op — Local Play, Remote Play and Mods','Choose Brotato local co-op or Steam Remote Play Together. Check the host, devices and current version before using old multiplayer mod instructions.', 'Steam lists shared-screen co-op and Remote Play Together. For friends elsewhere, Remote Play Together streams a host’s local session. Start with the supported route before seeking a multiplayer mod.', 'base',[
('choose','Choose for your devices',table(['Situation','Route','Check first'],[['One screen','Local co-op','Connect and join with the intended input devices.'],['Friends elsewhere on Steam','Remote Play Together','One host runs the game and invites guests.'],['Independent console copies','Platform-specific features','Steam streaming support does not establish cross-console matchmaking.'],['Old mod tutorial','Check date and game version','The instructions may predate supported local co-op.']])+p(link(BASE,'Brotato Steam features')+' and '+link('https://store.steampowered.com/remoteplay','Valve’s Remote Play guide')+' establish the Steam routes.')),
('remote','Set up Remote Play Together','<ol><li>The host launches the installed Steam game.</li><li>Invite the guest using Remote Play Together in the Steam friends list or overlay.</li><li>The guest accepts. Check allowed controller and keyboard inputs.</li><li>Join the local session and confirm each player controls a different character before starting.</li></ol>'+p('Valve documents one owner running the game while guests receive video and return inputs. The host computer and connection remain involved.')),
('trouble','If inputs or crates fail',p('When two people control one character, check Remote Play input permissions and local device assignment separately. Establish that controllers work locally before blaming the connection.')+p('After an update, reproduce crashes without mods. The November 3 patch includes a Survivor co-op crate fix. The 12 November default-branch patch fixes the Mecha Parts counter blocking co-op shop and inventory navigation. Match the symptom and branch before assuming a particular issue is fixed. '+link(NEWS,'Official patch notes'))),
('beta','Check weapon-popup navigation after updating',p('The 12 November default-branch patch fixes controller navigation getting stuck in a weapon popup when buttons are hidden. Hotfix 1.2.0.3 also fixes the missing gamepad selection after buying an item while the mouse cursor rests on another shop item. Check the installed branch when matching this symptom to a patch note. '+link(BALANCE,'12 November balance notes'))),
('next','Check the session before a long run',p('Agree on host, inputs and enabled content. Start a short unmodded session to verify controls. We have not tested remote parties, console pairings or shared progression. For mod conflicts, use the <a href="/brotato/mods/">compatibility checklist</a>.'))]),
('updates','Brotato Updates — New Dawn, 1.2 and the Beta Branch','Identify the update a Brotato guide describes. Separate New Dawn, free Item Sets, Primal Dread and November beta balance notes.', 'New Dawn, update 1.2 and Primal Dread are different content labels. The 12 November Steam Balancing Patch brings the tested Evolution changes to the default branch. Use Item Sets to check enabled content.', 'item-set',[
('labels','Match the label to the task',table(['Label','Practical meaning'],[['New Dawn','A separately listed update in Item Sets. Match its toggle when reproducing older content.'],['Update 1.2','Free Item Set menu, older-character and Nightmare adjustments.'],['Primal Dread','Paid expansion with Jungle and Evolution.'],['1.2.0.1','November 3 post-launch patch.'],['1.2.0.2.beta-0','November 6 optional balance beta.'],['1.2.0.2.beta-1','November 10 optional beta, with further Evolution, shop and Jungle changes.'],['12 November Balancing Patch','Tested Evolution changes released on the Steam default branch.'],['1.2.0.3','13 November hotfix: Caveman starting weapon reversal, Snowball mutation fix and gamepad/foot fixes.']])+p(link(NEWS,'Developer update history')+' documents the November changes.')),
('sets','Reproduce a guide with Item Sets',p('The 1.2 announcement introduces switches for expansions and free updates. It gives disabling Paws & Claws while leaving other content active as an example. Open Item Sets from Character Selection and compare the setup with the guide.')+p('If a weapon never appears, inspect enabled content before spending more rerolls. Installed content and enabled content are separate checks.')),
('beta','Check optional participation',p('Steam Library → Brotato → Properties → Betas shows participation. The 6 November announcement separates balancing from the default branch. It says this balance beta retains progression when changes move to main, and asks players to deactivate and unsubscribe from Workshop mods. '+link(NEWS,'Beta instructions'))+p('That progression statement applies to this announced beta. Keep your own backup before an experimental setup.')),
('balance','Check the current default-branch rules',p('The 12 November Balancing Patch releases the tested changes for Steam players. Gain one ban token every four waves through wave 20. Mutation effects reach 70% strength at 40 Evolution and full strength at 100. Mechanization loses extra piercing and bounces. The announcement also rebalances Jungle waves and fixes co-op shop navigation. '+link(BALANCE,'Official release notes'))+p('The publisher plans another weapon-balancing patch. Match future build advice to the installed version and record your active Item Sets.')),
('hotfix','Match hotfix 1.2.0.3 to the symptom',p('The 13 November hotfix removes Boomerang from Caveman’s starting weapons. Snowball gains Elemental Damage from purchased or crate items, while Tumor mutations stop granting extra Elemental Damage. Weapons can now target and hit the Brachiosaurus foot, and the wave-end foot crash receives a fix for death and victory. A gamepad shop-selection issue and moving Ammosaurus attacks are also fixed. '+link(HOTFIX,'Official 1.2.0.3 notes'))),
('report','Report a useful discrepancy',p('Include exact version, branch, map, difficulty, active sets and mods. A tooltip screenshot helps establish which rule you actually have. Use '+link('https://steamcommunity.com/app/1942280/discussions/1/','the developer-linked bug forum')+' for reproducible issues.'))]),
('mods','Brotato Mods After 1.2 — Compatibility Checklist','Check Workshop mods against Brotato 1.2, distinguish beta instructions and reproduce crashes before installing old multiplayer loaders.', 'Reproduce crashes without mods after updating to 1.2. The developer warns that outdated mods can conflict. The November balance beta additionally asks players to deactivate and unsubscribe from Workshop mods.', 'item-set',[
('baseline','Establish the clean baseline','<ol><li>Record version, branch and subscriptions.</li><li>Back up your save before changing an experimental setup.</li><li>Deactivate mods and restart.</li><li>Repeat the failing action with the same character and Item Sets.</li><li>Check current patch notes if it still fails.</li></ol>'+p(link(NEWS,'Developer launch and beta warnings')+' support this first diagnostic step. A continuing unmodded crash needs its own reproduction report.')),
('return','Restore a compatible setup',p('Check each author’s supported version, dependencies and recent comments. Restore one compatible mod or required dependency group, restart and repeat the failing action before adding another. Workshop popularity does not establish compatibility.')+p('The 12 November balance changes are released on the Steam default branch. Record your installed version and patch date when comparing a mod author’s supported builds. For the November beta, follow the developer’s deactivate-and-unsubscribe instruction. If a required mod supports only the default branch, use that supported environment.')),
('coop','Check whether a multiplayer mod is needed',p('Steam lists local co-op and Remote Play Together. Older loader tutorials may predate those features. For a normal run with friends, use the <a href="/brotato/co-op/">supported co-op setup</a> first. Identify the extra feature you need before choosing a mod.')),
('report','When the clean game still crashes',p('Compare the exact action against the November 3 Survivor co-op crate fix and hotfix 1.2.0.3, which fixes a wave-end crash while the Brachiosaurus foot is active on death or victory. The November 12 patch also adjusts modding internals for robustness, but each mod still needs its own compatibility check. A matching note is a reason to update and retry. Report version, steps and crash details if it persists. We have not validated individual packages or a universal crash fix.'))]),
('vs-vampire-survivors','Brotato vs Vampire Survivors — Choose Your Run Style','Compare Brotato and Vampire Survivors by shopping rhythm, build choices and playing with friends. Find the setup guide for your group.', 'Choose Brotato for repeated short combat waves with shop decisions between them. Choose Vampire Survivors for an extended stage run shaped by level-up choices and evolution recipes. Check the exact multiplayer mode separately.', 'base',[
('rhythm','Choose the rhythm of your decisions',table(['Preference','Starting fit','Why'],[['Frequent stops to plan purchases','Brotato','Buying, locking and rerolling sit between combat waves.'],['Continuous stage progression','Vampire Survivors','Level-up choices and evolution conditions shape the run.'],['Weapon copies and character restrictions','Brotato','The loadout develops through a character-specific shop plan.'],['Evolution combinations','Vampire Survivors','A recipe and its conditions provide a distinct progression task.']])+p('This is an editorial fit comparison based on the '+link(BASE,'Brotato description')+' and '+link('https://store.steampowered.com/app/1794680/Vampire_Survivors/','Vampire Survivors description')+'. It is not a performance benchmark.')),
('friends','Plan the group setup',p('Brotato’s Steam features include local co-op and Remote Play Together. Remote Play streams a host session. Vampire Survivors has its own mode and platform requirements. Enter your actual devices into the choice process using the <a href="/vampire-survivors/co-op/">Vampire Survivors co-op guide</a> and <a href="/brotato/co-op/">Brotato setup guide</a>.')),
('dlc','Understand the base loop first',p('If you are new to both games, learn the base loop before selecting expansion content. Brotato’s Item Sets let owners disable content to reproduce a simpler run. Primal Dread adds another decision layer through Evolution and changes enemy hazards.')),
('choose','Pick the first session',p('Choose Brotato for frequent pauses to compare purchases. Choose Vampire Survivors for planning progression through a stage. If group play decides the purchase, agree on screens, host and platforms first. Check current prices for your store and region.'))])]
